WEBVTT

00:02:28.686 --> 00:02:31.647
and produce new offspring every six weeks.

00:02:31.647 --> 00:02:34.400
They actually have higher breeding rates
in cities

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.694
because of the abundance 
of food and shelter.

00:02:37.111 --> 00:02:40.489
These booming populations 
attract predators.

00:02:40.489 --> 00:02:43.034
New York City is home 
to a million pigeons,

00:02:43.034 --> 00:02:46.078
which support large populations
of raptors.

00:02:46.078 --> 00:02:47.997
But pigeons’ aptitude for swift flight,

00:02:47.997 --> 00:02:50.249
further exploited by being bred
for racing,

00:02:50.249 --> 00:02:53.127
means they’re made 
for high speed chases.

00:02:53.127 --> 00:02:55.838
Compared to barn owls,
which are a similar size,

00:02:55.838 --> 00:02:58.257
pigeon wing bones are thicker 
and more curved,

00:02:58.257 --> 00:03:00.384
providing extra space for muscle mass.